ef 17592186045417] [17592186246957 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e597727d-4abc-5787-967c-bd4759284ec9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5c48c40-2fd0-5515-867f-1f3be83f3dfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247306 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c8b3d18-f99b-57ac-806c-9402fb0d526b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247309 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the equations, we get  \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}={b}_{1}+2(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2})-3(-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{1}-12{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319532 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319532 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319532 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c1f3a69-7740-5aa2-925c-53c1ce3286b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319705 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319705 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319705 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66b1a873-459f-552e-a7e5-027c42c7521c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319799 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319799 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319799 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8891e75e-27cb-5964-9e25-018084c2ca28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319862 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{6}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319862 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319862 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d0ae0bb-3fdb-536c-87d0-6e5d6c437047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320002 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{align