_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. By adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1045 "Writing Vectors in Different Bases" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186424440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424423 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f5cbb860-2adf-582c-a552-bdba6343726b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424424 #edb/ref 1080 "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424424 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424424 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11a1b0ee-a4a2